SUMMARY:Rock & Roll Playhouse: The Music of The Grateful Dead & More
DESCRIPTION:The Rock and Roll Playhouse\, a family concert series hosted at historic music venues across the country\, allows kids to “move\, play and sing while listening to works from the classic-rock canon” (NY Times). Performing songs created by the most iconic musicians in rock history\, The Rock and Roll Playhouse band offers its core audience of families with children age ten and under games\, movement\, stories and an opportunity to rock out in an effort to educate children and explore their creativity. The Rock and Roll Playhouse is an early and often first introduction to a child’s lifelong journey with live music and rock and roll. This children’s concert is not associated with or endorsed by the artist. This concert for kids and families shares the music of the artist named above with a new generation of music lovers\, but is not associated with or endorsed by the artist. All children (over age 1) must have a ticket and be accompanied by a parent or adult caregiver. \nChildren under 1 free! \nThe Rock and Roll Playhouse knows that little ears are sensitive\, so we turn down the volume at our shows. However\, all kids experience music differently and you may find that your child is more comfortable wearing hearing protection earmuffs\, such as Baby Banz.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/rock-roll-playhouse-the-music-of-the-grateful-dead-more/
LOCATION:Motorco\, 723 Rigsbee\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Kid At Heart,Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/20260621_gratefulDead_promo_1080x1080-1-2.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Motorco":MAILTO:noreply@facebookmail.com
GEO:36.003527;-78.900332
